# Append-only shared logs: every writer adds at EOF, so two branches that both append
# conflict on the SAME final hunk every time. README.md law 2 says "Merge conflicts are
# impossible by construction" -- that holds only for writers appending directly to master.
# The fleet uses branches (review/*, codex/*, claude/*), and TRAPS.md alone takes ~480 added
# lines/day, so in practice this conflicted on essentially every branch that recorded a trap.
#
# `union` is git's built-in driver for exactly this shape: on conflict it keeps BOTH sides'
# lines rather than raising. That is the correct resolution for an append-only log and it is
# what a human does by hand anyway. It does NOT make edits safe -- if two branches rewrite the
# same existing line, union keeps both copies -- which is fine here precisely because these
# files are append-only by doctrine. Corrections are appended as new CORRECTION entries, never
# by editing the entry being corrected.
TRAPS.md        merge=union
RECEIPTS.md     merge=union
RULINGS.md      merge=union
DISCOVERIES.md  merge=union

# Generated, never hand-edited: regenerate with `python tools/traps-index.py --write` rather
# than resolving it. Union would interleave two derived tables into nonsense.
TRAPS-INDEX.md  -merge
